From 6d6bb4a51af190eee40f86e9306f5c249472eade Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Medium1992 <Medium1992@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 22:27:45 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 35/35] XHTTP: Forward a limited flow governor server no more
 unused credit than before

A server with a send window shows its own stack 16 KiB for the client's
initial window where it showed 65535, so for the same window it forwarded
49151 bytes more. Credit the stack has not used is what a client's lowering
of its initial window cannot take back: a lowering to 200000 on a new stream
could be passed on before and closed the connection now.

The stack is now forwarded no more ahead of the data it has sent than it had
unused with 65535 shown. A stream opens with 49151 bytes less in its window
and has all of it once data moves. A stream whose stack has sent all it was
forwarded needs no value that low, and such a lowering is passed on now.
